    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0299" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg293"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 148.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                                1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reference to the carrying out of
                    Articles VIII and IX of the Joint Note of December 22 last, the previous
                    correspondence concerning which I transmitted you in my dispatches Nos. 69, of
                    April 16, and 143, of July 27, 1901, I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    your information a note addressed by the dean of the diplomatic corps to the
                    Chinese plenipotentiaries under date of July 28 giving a list of the
                    fortifications which are to be razed, and another, from the same to the same,
                    stating the points which will be held by foreign troops to protect the lines of
                    communication between the capital and the sea.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>




